            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For a wall that moves or cracks, yes — an elastomeric membrane stretches across a hairline crack where DRYLOK's rigid film splits along with it. For a stable interior wall being finished as living space, DRYLOK is the better choice: it costs less per square foot, it can be tinted or painted over, and it is rated to 15 psi of hydrostatic pressure.",
