            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Liquid rubber. Elastomeric membranes are formulated for below-grade exterior use, cure seamlessly with no laps for water to track behind, and stay flexible through freeze-thaw movement. DRYLOK is primarily an interior masonry waterproofer. If you are already excavating, the exterior face is the correct side to waterproof.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can you paint over liquid rubber?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Generally no. The cured surface stays rubbery and flexible, and ordinary wall paint will not adhere to it or will crack as the membrane moves. A finished room over liquid rubber needs framing and board rather than paint. DRYLOK, by contrast, is tintable and accepts a masonry-suitable topcoat once cured.",
          },
        },
