            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Liquid rubber, by a clear margin per square foot. It is a high-solids product applied thickly, so a gallon covers far less area than a gallon of DRYLOK, and it costs more per gallon to begin with. On a full basement perimeter the difference is significant, which is why liquid rubber is usually reserved for the walls that actually need flexibility.",
