          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Do you still need to fill cracks first?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For DRYLOK, always — it seals pores rather than bridging gaps, so an unfilled crack simply cracks the coating. Liquid rubber bridges hairline cracks by design, but anything wider than a hairline, and any actively leaking crack, still needs hydraulic cement or a polyurethane injection before the membrane goes on.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: authorSchema(),
      datePublished: dates.published,
      dateModified: dates.modified,
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "The Honest Reviewers" },
